# Line endings are part of the bytes, and this repository makes byte-level claims.
#
# GRT-080 asserts that viewer/public/frames/nyc-harbor-enu.json is a byte-for-byte copy of the
# canonical frame published by digital-3d-shared-contracts. Without this file, git checks that JSON
# out with CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux, the two hash differently, and the test passes on a
# developer's machine while failing in CI -- which is exactly what happened on the first Pages run.
# Line-ending translation IS a re-serialisation, and the contract says do not re-serialise.
#
# Everything textual is therefore normalised to LF in the repository AND in the working tree, so the
# hash is the same everywhere and a rebuild on any platform is byte-identical to what is committed.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated model artifacts: text, but never hand-edited. Same LF rule applies so that a rebuild
# produces no spurious diff.
*.json text eol=lf
*.gltf text eol=lf

# Binaries: never translated, never diffed as text.
*.glb binary
*.bin binary
*.pdf binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.avif binary
*.ply binary
*.blend binary
*.step binary
